{
  "slug": "cmux-ultimate",
  "name": "Cmux Ultimate",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Complete cmux integration for Claude Code. Includes full CLI reference (~130 commands), browser automation (~40 subcommands with element refs), multi-agent orchestration patterns, sidebar metadata, lifecycle hooks (auto workspace naming, active/idle status, completion notifications), and two slash commands (/cmux:status, /cmux:open-browser). Built by combining the best features from four existing cmux plugins into one cohesive package.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill**, **2 commands** and **3 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (1): `cmux` (cmux CLI reference for Claude Code: workspace/pane/surface management, browser automation, multi-agent orchestration, sidebar metadata, notifications, and tmux migration)\n- **Commands** (2): `open-browser` (Open a browser split pane to a URL and report what's visible), `status` (Show current cmux workspace status — surfaces, panes, sidebar state)\n- **Hooks** (3): `SessionStart`, `Stop`, `Notification`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install cmux-ultimate@claude-community` from `AndrewPalet/cmux-ultimate`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 1,
    "hook": 3,
    "command": 2
  },
